# Wave W17-T (Route 130): quiet sand — glass-clear shallows sand: a pale bright shore sand carrying garden flecks — soft green and coral-pink hints standing sparse in the tread, the CORALET gardens showing through the shallows in the sand\u2019s own art (design: gardens visible through glass-clear water on every side of the gentle lane — water dressing drawn in the sand kind, art layer only; the shipped coral cells themselves stand byte-preserved). Route 130\u2019s own sand — the fleet\u2019s only garden-flecked sand: split from Route 129\u2019s pale lee sand (calm, unmarked — nothing shows through the lee) by the garden colours themselves, and from Route 127\u2019s kelp-shadowed sand by register (garden light vs forest shadow).
